# Copy to `.env` and fill in. The real `.env` is gitignored — never commit cookies or keys.
#   cp .env.example .env

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by the backend (app.config.Settings) and by Alembic.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://fbb:fbb@localhost:5433/fbb

# Consumed by docker-compose to provision the local Postgres 16 container.
# Keep these in sync with DATABASE_URL above.
POSTGRES_USER=fbb
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=fbb
POSTGRES_DB=fbb
# Host port the container is published on. 5433 avoids clashing with a local
# Postgres install on 5432; keep it in sync with DATABASE_URL.
POSTGRES_PORT=5433

# --- Access (the shared password) -------------------------------------------
# The one token that gates the whole API, and the only auth this tool has: one password, two
# people, no accounts (backend/app/auth.py). UNSET MEANS OFF — leave it commented out locally
# and every endpoint answers, which is what `make test` and `make backend` expect.
#
# SET IT ON ANY DEPLOYMENT. Every endpoint here can write — reorder the master board, edit a
# draft pick, re-import a projection — so a public URL without this is a board anyone can
# rewrite. Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 24`, and keep it ASCII: an HTTP header carries
# bytes, so a password with an accent in it is one no browser can send.
#
# `/`, `/health` and `/health/db` stay open whatever this is set to, so a platform health check
# and the frontend's status strip work before anyone has typed a password. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
# APP_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- ESPN league access -----------------------------------------------------
# Private-league auth: copy these two cookies from your browser while logged in
# to fantasy.espn.com. They expire periodically and need re-pasting.
ESPN_S2=paste_espn_s2_cookie_here
SWID={PASTE-SWID-COOKIE-HERE}
ESPN_LEAGUE_ID=123456789
ESPN_SEASON=2026

# --- Player ages ------------------------------------------------------------
# The date ages are computed as of. Ages are derived from nba.com birthdates, and are
# deliberately NOT computed from "today": a stored age has to be reproducible between runs and
# correct on draft day. Defaults to Oct 1 of the season ESPN_SEASON starts (ESPN_SEASON=2027
# is the 2026-27 season, so 2026-10-01). Set it explicitly to pin ages to another date.
# AGE_AS_OF=2026-10-01

# --- Dynasty age/longevity curve --------------------------------------------
# The whole dynasty adjustment: one multiplier on a player's current-year value, as five
# numbers. The prime band multiplies 1.0; each year under it adds the youth bonus, each year
# over it subtracts the decline, and the floor is where the discount stops. Defaults below are
# a MODERATE curve — a starting point to calibrate, not a conviction. `GET /valuation/curve`
# prints the active params and an age -> multiplier table. Value is computed on read, so a
# change here re-ranks the board on the next request; nothing needs re-importing.
# DYNASTY_PRIME_START=24
# DYNASTY_PRIME_END=27
# DYNASTY_YOUTH_BONUS_PER_YEAR=0.04
# DYNASTY_DECLINE_PER_YEAR=0.05
# DYNASTY_MIN_MULTIPLIER=0.40

# --- Draft tiers -------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto-tiering by score-gap clustering: a new tier opens wherever the drop to the next player
# is more than TIER_GAP_MULTIPLE times the MEDIAN drop across the tiered pool. Median, so the
# cliffs at the top of the board don't inflate the bar and swallow the ordinary breaks below
# them. Higher multiple -> fewer, larger tiers. TIER_MIN_SIZE keeps singletons out (bar a
# genuinely huge gap), TIER_MAX caps the count (merging the least significant breaks first),
# and TIER_POOL is how many top-ranked players get tiered at all — everyone below is untiered.
# `GET /valuation/tiers` prints the active params and every break on the live board. Tiers are
# computed on read, like value, so a change here re-cuts the board on the next request.
# TIER_GAP_MULTIPLE=2.0
# TIER_MIN_SIZE=2
# TIER_MAX=15
# TIER_POOL=150

# --- Market lines ------------------------------------------------------------
# Season-long sportsbook props -> a fair per-game number, then a market projection priced
# under our scoring (`make import KIND=market_line ...`). MARKET_SIGMA_FRAC is the only free
# parameter in the odds model: the per-stat dispersion as a fraction of the line itself
# (sigma = frac * max(line, 1.0)). It scales how far a SHADED price moves the value away from
# the line; an even, one-sided or missing price leaves value == line at every setting, so this
# dial can never turn a bare line into something other than that line. Higher -> juiced odds
# move the number further. Unlike the curve and the tiers, a change here needs a re-import to
# take effect: market values are DERIVED at import time into a projection row, not on read.
# MARKET_SIGMA_FRAC=0.25
# Games to multiply a market player's per-game value by when ESPN has no projected-games count
# for him. Display only — the board ranks on per-game.
# MARKET_DEFAULT_GAMES=70

# --- Master ranking board ----------------------------------------------------
# Which consensus OUR board (`GET /master/board`) is seeded from on its first read, and whose
# pool decides who belongs on it at all. Note what it is NOT: the horizon of the board. There
# is one board, arranged by hand and kept; `?horizon=` on the endpoint only chooses which
# consensus the REFERENCE column beside each rank is computed against. Pinning membership here
# is what stops reading the board through the win-now lens from quietly admitting a hundred
# players who are only on a redraft list. A win-now league would set current_year.
# MASTER_SEED_HORIZON=dynasty

# --- Frontend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend base URL the Next.js app calls. Must be NEXT_PUBLIC_ to reach the browser, and it is
# baked in at BUILD time — on Vercel, changing it needs a redeploy. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Optional: CORS ---------------------------------------------------------
# The origins allowed to call the API. Defaults to the Next dev server, which is why this is
# commented out for local work. Two accepted forms — comma-separated, which is what a hosting
# dashboard wants, or the JSON array:
#   CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-project.vercel.app,https://your-project-git-main-you.vercel.app
#   CORS_ORIGINS=["http://localhost:3000"]
# Scheme and host only: no trailing slash, no path. An EMPTY value allows no origin at all
# rather than falling back to the default — that would look like the setting had worked.
# CORS_ORIGINS=["http://localhost:3000"]

# --- Future: odds / stats providers (not wired up yet) ----------------------
# BALLDONTLIE_API_KEY=
# THE_ODDS_API_KEY=
